00:03:27.159 --> 00:03:31.680
But this is not unique to Donald Trump and
I think it bears a little more exploration.

00:03:31.680 --> 00:03:36.469
And to understand this, you have to think
about personal versus in group priorities,

00:03:36.469 --> 00:03:39.030
personal versus in-group frameworks.

00:03:39.030 --> 00:03:42.779
The 2010 Tea Party is an example that I've
talked about before.

00:03:42.779 --> 00:03:45.230
Social psychologist Jonathan Haidt talked
about this.

00:03:45.230 --> 00:03:48.760
We interviewed him on the program a year or
so ago, maybe a little longer.

00:03:48.760 --> 00:03:50.370
And he's written about this extensively.

00:03:50.370 --> 00:03:53.700
He wrote about it in the book The Righteous
Mind, which if you don't have to agree with

00:03:53.700 --> 00:03:58.700
everything that Jonathan Haidt writes but
and I don't agree with it 100 percent, but

00:03:58.700 --> 00:04:01.120
he writes about this extensively.

00:04:01.120 --> 00:04:08.459
And the gist is when you look at individual
versus group framing, there is a very long

00:04:08.459 --> 00:04:15.159
history of people acting in ways that don't
seem to be optimized at their individual level,

00:04:15.159 --> 00:04:17.269
but are optimized for their group.

00:04:17.269 --> 00:04:21.530
And as a result, they perceive that it will
confer benefits to them.

00:04:21.530 --> 00:04:24.960
And the best way to think about it is with
an example.

00:04:24.960 --> 00:04:26.630
You look at the 2010 Tea Party.

00:04:26.630 --> 00:04:27.630
All right.

00:04:27.630 --> 00:04:31.470
2010 Tea Party ran on lower taxes for the
rich.

00:04:31.470 --> 00:04:32.470
Don't tread on me.

00:04:32.470 --> 00:04:33.470
Right?

00:04:33.470 --> 00:04:37.140
So lower government regulations, lower government
involvement, don't regulate business nearly

00:04:37.140 --> 00:04:38.140
as much.

00:04:38.140 --> 00:04:44.070
Essentially allow more pollution, lower fuel
efficiency standards, more oil drilling, fewer

00:04:44.070 --> 00:04:46.820
welfare benefits and social programs.

00:04:46.820 --> 00:04:50.100
You look at who was overwhelmingly supporting
the Tea Party.

00:04:50.100 --> 00:04:55.140
You look at the districts where the Tea Party
candidate won sometimes against an incumbent,

00:04:55.140 --> 00:04:58.000
sort of more traditional Republican.

00:04:58.000 --> 00:05:02.220
It was overwhelmingly people who were never
going to be rich and benefit from those tax

00:05:02.220 --> 00:05:07.000
cuts for the rich whose taxes weren't going
to go down if Tea Partiers got their way,

00:05:07.000 --> 00:05:11.950
who live in places that would be ravaged by
the very industrial pollution that the Tea

00:05:11.950 --> 00:05:16.470
Party would have allowed by eliminating government
regulations and taking this laissez faire

00:05:16.470 --> 00:05:18.320
more libertarian approach.

00:05:18.320 --> 00:05:22.280
So you might be able to just simply say, we're
on the left.

00:05:22.280 --> 00:05:25.970
We we we understand what these dumb people
don't.

00:05:25.970 --> 00:05:31.120
These are just stupid people tricked into
voting against their own best interests.

00:05:31.120 --> 00:05:33.050
And that is so the wrong approach.

00:05:33.050 --> 00:05:38.150
They may have been tricked, but it's not that
they don't understand the policies of the

00:05:38.150 --> 00:05:39.150
Tea Party.

00:05:39.150 --> 00:05:42.200
They understand in many cases what the policies
are.

00:05:42.200 --> 00:05:49.210
They've identified that those are the policies
that their group favors, even if they don't

00:05:49.210 --> 00:05:54.000
immediately see or believe that at any point
they will personally benefit.

00:05:54.000 --> 00:05:57.270
They believe that there will be a sort of
trickle down benefit because this is what

00:05:57.270 --> 00:05:58.770
their group wants.

00:05:58.770 --> 00:06:02.220
And that is why they are voting for these
policies by voting for the Tea Party.

00:06:02.220 --> 00:06:03.460
They may not even know why.

00:06:03.460 --> 00:06:07.490
They may not realize that their group has
actually been taken over by elites who want

00:06:07.490 --> 00:06:11.390
to use them as a tool to achieve what's good
for them rather than for the actual voters

00:06:11.390 --> 00:06:14.060
who are just gonna get peanuts or crumbs.

00:06:14.060 --> 00:06:18.890
But they understand the policies and in many
cases they've identified the policies as this

00:06:18.890 --> 00:06:22.750
is what our team or our group wants.

00:06:22.750 --> 00:06:26.640
And I'm going to vote with the orthodoxy of
the group I'm a part of.

00:06:26.640 --> 00:06:31.890
Apply that to the Trump voter and you see
that there is a similarity in many cases we've

00:06:31.890 --> 00:06:35.080
categorized Trump voters before.

00:06:35.080 --> 00:06:38.050
Some of them don't actually understand what
Trump right ran on.

00:06:38.050 --> 00:06:42.190
They don't they have no clue what the policies
are or they don't understand them.

00:06:42.190 --> 00:06:44.290
